{{Use mdy dates|date=May 2023}}
{{USTV|2023}}
The '''2023–24 network television schedule''' for the five major English-language commercial [[List of United States over-the-air television networks|broadcast networks in the United States]] covers the [[prime time]] hours from September 2023 to August 2024. The schedule is followed by a [[#By network|list per network]] of returning series, new series, and series canceled after the [[2022–23 United States network television schedule|2022–23 television season]]. The schedule was affected by strikes undertaken by the [[2023 Writers Guild of America strike|Writers Guild of America]] (which began on May 2 and ended on September 27)<ref>{{Cite web|last1=Littleton|first1=Cynthia|last2=Aurthur|first2=Kate|last3=Donnelly|first3=Matt|last4=Maddaus|first4=Gene|title=Deal! WGA, AMPTP Reach Historic Contract Agreement to End 146-Day Writers Strike: 'This Deal Is Exceptional'|url=https://variety.com/2023/biz/news/writers-strike-ends-wga-amptp-deal-2-1235733452/|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=September 25, 2023}}</ref> and [[2023 SAG-AFTRA strike|SAG-AFTRA]] (which began on July 14 and ended on November 9). Programming impacts on the 2023–24 season itself were limited in comparison to previous television seasons affected by [[2023 Hollywood labor disputes|Hollywood labor disputes]].

[[CBS]] was the first to announce its initial fall schedule on May 10, 2023, via press release (without an [[Upfront (advertising)|upfront]] presentation). However, as a result of the ongoing strikes, a revised schedule for CBS was released on July 17 (with its premiere dates announced on August 3).<ref name="CBS Fall 2023">{{Cite press release|title=CBS Reveals Its 2023–2024 Primetime Lineup|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/05/10/cbs-reveals-its-2023-2024-primetime-lineup-521213/20230510cbs01/|publisher=[[CBS]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=May 10, 2023}}</ref><ref name="CBS Fall 2023 Programming Update">{{Cite press release|title=CBS Announces Fall 2023 Programming|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/07/17/cbs-announces-fall-2023-programming-556110/20230717cbs01/|publisher=[[CBS]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=July 17, 2023}}</ref><ref name="CBS Fall 2023 Dates">{{Cite press release|title=CBS Announces Primetime Programming Premiere Dates for Fall 2023|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/08/03/cbs-announces-primetime-programming-premiere-dates-for-fall-2023-830213/20230803cbs01/|publisher=[[CBS]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=August 3, 2023}}</ref> This was followed by [[NBC]], which also announced its initial schedule on May 12 (with their upfront presentation at 11 a.m. [[Eastern Time Zone|Eastern Time]] on May 15), but later announced its revised schedule on July 19 and August 29 (along with the premiere dates),<ref name="NBC Fall 2023">{{Cite press release|title=NBC Anchors Fall Schedule with Franchise Powerhouses and Three New Series|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/05/12/nbc-anchors-fall-schedule-with-franchise-powerhouses-and-three-new-series-253113/20230512nbc01/|publisher=[[NBC]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=May 12, 2023}}</ref><ref name="NBC Fall Wednesday Update">{{Cite web|last=White|first=Peter|title=NBC Shuffles Wednesday Lineup On Fall Schedule — Update|url=https://deadline.com/2023/08/nbc-fall-schedule-magnum-pi-quantum-leap-found-the-irrational-1235441741/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=August 29, 2023|access-date=August 30, 2023}}</ref> and [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] which announced its initial schedule on May 16 (with their upfront presentation at 4 p.m. that day) but later announced part of its revised schedule (along with its premiere dates on August 21), with its Tuesday and Monday schedule (along with its premiere dates) on September 12 and 18 respectively.<ref name="ABC Fall 2023">{{Cite press release|title=ABC, No. 1 in Entertainment for Fourth Consecutive Season, Announces 2023–2024 Fall Primetime Schedule Featuring Strong Slate of Fan-Favorite Programming With Originals Debuting Every Night|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/05/16/abc-no-1-in-entertainment-for-fourth-consecutive-season-announces-2023-2024-fall-primetime-schedule-featuring-strong-slate-of-fan-favorite-programming-with-originals-debuting-every-night-744115/20230516abc01/|publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=May 16, 2023}}</ref><ref name="ABC Fall 2023 Premiere Dates">{{Cite press release|title=ABC Announces Revised Fall Schedule, Sets Premiere Dates|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/08/21/abc-announces-revised-fall-schedule-sets-premiere-dates-786511/20230821abc01/|publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=August 21, 2023}}</ref><ref name="DancingPremiere">{{Cite web|last=Swift|first=Andy|title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Sets Season 32 Premiere Date — See ABC's (Almost) Complete Fall Schedule|url=https://www.tvline.com/news/dancing-with-the-stars-season-32-release-date-abc-fall-2023-schedule-1235041674/|website=[[TVLine]]|date=September 12, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Lewis|first=Jon|title=ABC to air MNF every week for rest of season|url=https://www.sportsmediawatch.com/2023/09/abc-airing-monday-night-football-all-season-due-to-writers-strike/|website=Sports Media Watch|date=September 18, 2023|access-date=September 22, 2023}}</ref> [[The CW]] announced its initial fall schedule on May 18 (their upfront presentation of the original schedule was held at 11 a.m. that day), before it was revised on June 6 with the release of its summer schedule for the previous season, and its replacement programming was announced on July 12 (along with their premiere dates).<ref>{{Cite press release|title=The CW Network Sets Summer 2023 Premiere Dates|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/06/07/the-cw-network-sets-summer-2023-premiere-dates-154412/20230607cw02/|publisher=[[The CW]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=June 7, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite press release|title=The CW Network Scores Exclusive Broadcast and Streaming Rights to Emmy Award-Winning Series "Inside the NFL"|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/06/07/the-cw-network-scores-exclusive-broadcast-and-streaming-rights-to-emmy-award-winning-series-inside-the-nfl-420315/20230607cw01/|publisher=[[The CW]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=June 7, 2023}}</ref><ref name="CWFallPremiereDates">{{Cite web|last=Petski|first=Denise|title=The CW Sets Fall Premiere Dates For ''The Swarm'', ''FBoy Island'' ''Inside The NFL'', More; ''All American'', ''61st Street'' Move To Midseason|url=https://deadline.com/2023/07/the-cw-fall-premiere-dates-the-swarm-fboy-island-inside-the-nfl-all-american-midseason-1235435797/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=July 12, 2023}}</ref><ref name="CW Fall 2023">{{Cite press release|title=The CW Network Announces Its Seven-Night Primetime Schedule for 2023–2024|url=http://thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/05/18/the-cw-network-announces-its-seven-night-primetime-schedule-for-2023-2024-198202/20230518cw01/|publisher=[[The CW]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=May 18, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Weprin|first=Alex|title=2023 Upfronts Schedule Set as Fox Plans In-Person Presentation at the Manhattan Center|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/2023-upfronts-schedule-set-dates-times-1235332630/|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=February 23, 2023|access-date=April 11, 2023}}</ref> [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]] announced its programming on May 15 via press release that morning (with their upfront presentation at 4 p.m. that day), but released its Sunday schedule (along with its release dates) on July 10, along with the rest of its prime-time schedule (which was revised  due to the strike, however its original schedule wasn't announced) (with their premiere dates) on July 11.<ref>{{Cite press release|title=Fox Entertainment Announces 2023–24 Program Slate with 6 New Series Orders, 5 Second Season Renewals and 13 Additional Series Returns|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/05/15/fox-entertainment-announces-2023-24-program-slate-with-6-new-series-orders-5-second-season-renewals-and-13-additional-series-returns-99004/20230515fox01/|publisher=[[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=May 15, 2023}}</ref><ref name="Fox Animation Domination Season Premiere Dates">{{Cite press release|title=Fox to Debut Animated Comedy "Krapopolis" on Sunday, Sept. 24|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/07/10/fox-to-debut-animated-comedy-krapopolis-on-sunday-sept-24-849013/20230710fox02/|publisher=[[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=July 10, 2023}}</ref><ref name="Fox Fall 2023">{{Cite press release|title=Fox Announces All Original Fall 2023 Slate with All-New Animated and Unscripted Series|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2023/07/11/fox-announces-all-original-fall-2023-slate-with-all-new-animated-and-unscripted-series-971012/20230711fox01/|publisher=[[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=July 11, 2023}}</ref>

This would be the first season that [[CBS News and Stations]] disaffiliated from The CW,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Miller |first=Mark |date=2023-06-14 |title=Nexstar Stations In Philadelphia, San Francisco, Tampa To Become CW Affils On Sept. 1 |url=https://tvnewscheck.com/business/article/nexstar-stations-in-philadelphia-san-francisco-tampa-to-become-cw-affils-on-sept-1/ |access-date=2023-09-01 |website=TV News Check |language=en}}</ref> as Paramount announced on May 5, 2023, that it would exercise the right with the transaction to disaffiliate all eight of their CW affiliates on September 1, 2023.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://deadline.com/2023/05/cbs-stations-eight-drop-cw-go-independent-this-fall-1235357388/|work=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]]|date=May 5, 2023|access-date=May 5, 2023|title=Eight CBS Stations To Ditch CW And Go Independent This Fall}}</ref> As a result, this would be the first season that [[Nexstar Media Group]] would be majority owner of The CW,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Miller |first=Mark |date=2022-08-15 |title=Nexstar Management Of CW Is Immediate |url=https://tvnewscheck.com/business/article/nexstar-management-of-cw-is-immediate/ |access-date=2023-06-15 |website=TVNewsCheck |language=en-US}}</ref> acquiring a 75-percent ownership stake; former joint owners [[Paramount Global]] and [[Warner Bros. Discovery]] retained a 25-percent stake, split at nominal 12.5-percent stakes for both companies.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hayes |first=Dade |date=October 3, 2022 |title=New Day Dawns For Broadcast TV As Nexstar Closes Deal For Control Of The CW |url=https://deadline.com/2022/10/nexstar-closes-deal-for-control-of-the-cw-mark-pedowitz-exits-top-job-1235133428/ |access-date=January 17, 2023 |website=Deadline |language=en-US |archive-date=October 14, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221014023432/https://deadline.com/2022/10/nexstar-closes-deal-for-control-of-the-cw-mark-pedowitz-exits-top-job-1235133428/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

[[PBS]] is not included, as member television stations have local flexibility over most of their schedule and broadcast times for network shows may vary. [[Ion Television]] and [[MyNetworkTV]] are also not included since both networks' schedules consist of syndicated reruns (with limited original programming).

Each of the 30 highest-rated shows released in May 2024 is listed with their ranks and ratings as determined by [[Nielsen Media Research]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Schneider|first=Michael|title=100 Most-Watched TV Series of 2023-24: This Season's Winners and Losers|url=https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/most-popular-tv-shows-highest-rated-2023-2024-season-tracker-survivor-1236015844/|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=May 28, 2024}}</ref>

Beginning this season, The CW began airing programming during the first hour of prime-time on Sundays.

== Impact of the 2023 Writers Guild of America and SAG-AFTRA strikes ==
{{Main|2023 Hollywood labor disputes}}
{{further|2023 Writers Guild of America strike|2023 SAG-AFTRA strike}}
On May 2, the [[Writers Guild of America]] went on strike, followed by [[SAG-AFTRA]] on July 13. The absence of working writers and actors through the summer led to scripted television production being shut down completely.<ref name="Variety">{{Cite web|last1=Otterson|first1=Joe|last2=Maas|first2=Jennifer|title=What SAG-AFTRA Strike Means for Summer Productions, Fall Premieres, Comic-Con and Q2 Earnings|url=https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/sag-strike-productions-fall-premieres-comic-con-q2-earnings-1235659448/|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=July 13, 2023|access-date=July 17, 2023}}</ref> The Writers Guild of America strike ended on September 27, while the SAG-AFTRA strike ended on November 9.

Network schedules were heavily altered in response to these strikes. The vast majority of new or returning live-action scripted series on the broadcast networks were delayed, pushing their premieres until 2024.<ref name="ABC Fall 2023"/><ref name="Fox Fall 2023"/><ref name="CWFallPremiereDates"/> Sports, [[reality shows]], and [[game shows]] filled many time slots as SAG-AFTRA members were permitted to work on such productions during the strike.<ref name="White"/><ref>{{Cite web|last=Maddeus|first=Gene|title=SAG-AFTRA Strike FAQ: How the Rules Apply to Influencers, Journalists, Cosplayers and More|url=https://variety.com/2023/biz/news/sag-strike-faq-rules-explainer-1235672265/|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=July 17, 2023}}</ref>

In other moves to work around the strikes, NBC delayed drama series ''[[Found (TV series)|Found]]'', which was originally intended to air as a mid-season replacement in the 2022–23 season, to fall 2023, while also fast-tracking the production of other scripted series such as the second season (of the revival, seventh overall) of ''[[Quantum Leap (2022 TV series)|Quantum Leap]]'' and the premiere season of ''[[The Irrational]]''.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Darwish|first=Meaghan|title=NBC Moves ''Found'' to Fall, Sets 2-Hour ''Magnum P.I.'' Premiere & Shifts ''The Blacklist''|url=https://www.tvinsider.com/1076890/found-series-premiere-fall-2023-magnum-pi-blacklist-schedule-nbc/|website=TV Insider|date=January 12, 2023|access-date=July 17, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Mulvey|first=Emily|title=''Quantum Leap'' Season 2 Could Feature Multiple Timelines|url=https://www.denofgeek.com/tv/quantum-leap-season-2-could-feature-multiple-timelines/|website=[[Den of Geek]]|date=April 5, 2023|access-date=July 17, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Petski|first=Denise|title=''The Irrational'' Drama Starring Jesse L. Martin Lands NBC Series Order|url=https://deadline.com/2022/12/the-irrational-drama-jesse-l-martin-nbc-series-order-1235207247/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=December 27, 2022|access-date=October 3, 2023}}</ref>

CBS aired series originally produced for sister properties, including ''[[Yellowstone (American TV series)|Yellowstone]]'' ([[Paramount Network]]), [[Paramount+]] shows ''[[SEAL Team (TV series)|SEAL Team]]'' (which originated on CBS) and  ''[[FBI True]]'', and ''[[NCIS: Sydney]]'', an Australian spin-off of ''[[NCIS (TV series)|NCIS]]'' originally intended for  Paramount+ and [[Network 10]] before being added to the CBS schedule as well.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|title=''NCIS: Sydney'' Gets Mothership Series' Longtime Tuesday Slot In CBS Scheduling Changes|url=https://deadline.com/2023/09/ncis-sydney-new-time-slot-tuesday-cbs-fall-schedule-changes-1235552709/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=September 21, 2023}}</ref><ref name="White">{{Cite web|last=White|first=Peter|title=''Yellowstone'' To Air On CBS' Reworked Fall Schedule Alongside Paramount+'s ''SEAL Team'', BBC's ''Ghosts'' & Reality-Heavy Slate|url=https://deadline.com/2023/07/cbs-fall-schedule-2023-yellowstone-ghosts-seal-team-fbi-true-1235439838/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=July 17, 2023}}</ref> Episodes of ''[[Ghosts (2019 British TV series)|Ghosts]]'', the BBC series on which [[Ghosts (American TV series)|the American adaptation]] was based, have also been added to the CBS schedule. Later in November, CBS announced that ''Matlock'' (a reboot of [[Matlock (1986 TV series)|the original 1980s series]] with a female lead), originally scheduled to air Sundays at 8 p.m., was forced to be moved to next season due to production delays.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|title=CBS Unveils Fall 2023 Schedule That Doesn't Factor In Strike Impact: 90-Minute ''Survivor'' & ''Amazing Race'', Newbies ''Matlock'' & ''Elsbeth''|url=https://deadline.com/2023/05/cbs-fall-2023-24-schedule-writers-strike-impact-survivor-amazing-race-matlock-elsbeth-1235361442/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=May 10, 2023|access-date=November 12, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Andreeva|first=Nellie|title=Most New Broadcast Scripted Series Moving To 2024–25 Season Due To Strike-Related Production Delays|url=https://deadline.com/2023/11/new-broadcast-series-move-2024-25-season-strike-metlock-dr-wolf-doc-rescue-hi-surf-poppas-house-st-denis-1235597159/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=November 9, 2023|access-date=November 12, 2023}}</ref><ref name="White" />

ABC aired additional sports coverage sourced from sister network [[ESPN]]. In the fall, ABC added 10 ''[[Monday Night Football]]'' games in simulcast with ESPN, on top of the seven simulcast or exclusive games previously scheduled.<ref>{{Cite news|title=ABC adds ''MNF'' simulcasts amid ongoing Hollywood writers strike|url=https://www.sportsbusinessjournal.com/Articles/2023/09/18/espn-abc-monday-night-football.aspx|work=[[Sports Business Journal]]|date=September 18, 2023}}</ref> In January 2024, ABC aired five [[National Basketball Association|NBA games]] on Wednesday nights that were originally scheduled to air on ESPN.<ref name="Lewis">{{Cite web|last=Lewis|first=Jon|title=ABC adds Wednesday night NBA games|url=https://www.sportsmediawatch.com/2023/10/abc-adds-nba-games-wednesday-nights-january-writers-strike/|website=Sports Media Watch|date=October 2, 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Lucia|first=Joe|title=ABC adding five Wednesday night NBA games in January from ESPN|url=https://awfulannouncing.com/nba/abc-five-wednesday-night-nba-games-january-espn.html|website=Awful Announcing|date=October 2, 2023|access-date=January 4, 2024}}</ref>

Fox stacked their schedule with unscripted series from Monday through Thursday nights, its Friday night (''[[WWE SmackDown]]'') and weekend sports programming was not affected. Its Sunday night animation lineup was also unaffected due to the long lead times required to produce such series.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Porter|first=Rick|title=Fox Execs on Strike-Impacted, Unscripted-Heavy Fall Launch: "We're Bullish"|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/fox-fall-2023-lineup-unscripted-strikes-1235588562/|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=September 13, 2023|access-date=October 3, 2023}}</ref> The CW is likewise relying more on unscripted programming as well as international acquisitions, though network executives stated that this was a long-term strategy shift following its acquisition by [[Nexstar Media Group|Nexstar]] rather than a specific reaction to the strike.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Cobb|first=Kayla|title=''All American'' Might Be the Only CW Series Impacted by Writers' Strike, President Says: 'We Knew We Had to Get Stuff Going'|url=https://www.thewrap.com/all-american-cw-impacted-by-wga-strike/|website=[[TheWrap]]|date=May 18, 2023|access-date=October 3, 2023}}</ref>

